$ABCD$ is a cyclic quadrilateral.
$\angle DAB = 108^{\circ}$.
Find $\angle BCD$.
[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{angles, quotes}
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (A) at (1.902,0.618);
\coordinate (B) at (1.766,0.939);
\coordinate (C) at (-1.995,-0.14);
\coordinate (D) at (-0.877,-1.798);
\draw (A) -- (B);
\draw (B) -- (C);
\draw (C) -- (D);
\draw (D) -- (A);
\draw (O) circle (2);
\node[right, xshift=3pt] at (A) {$A$};
\node[above] at (B) {$B$};
\node[left, xshift=-3pt] at (C) {$C$};
\node[below] at (D) {$D$};
\pic[draw, angle radius=0.45cm] {angle = B--A--D};
\node at (1.12,0.25) {$108^{\circ}$};
\pic[draw, "$x$", angle radius=0.45cm, angle eccentricity=2] {angle = D--C--B};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$ABCD$ is a cyclic quadrilateral, and side $BC$ is extended to $E$.
$\angle DCE = 93^{\circ}$.
Find $\angle DAB$.
[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{angles, quotes}
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (A) at (1.677,1.089);
\coordinate (B) at (1.147,1.638);
\coordinate (C) at (-2,-0.035);
\coordinate (D) at (-0.97,-1.749);
\draw (A) -- (B);
\draw (B) -- (C);
\draw (C) -- (D);
\draw (D) -- (A);
\draw (O) circle (2);
\coordinate (E) at (-3.888,-1.039);
\draw (C) -- (E);
\node[right, xshift=3pt] at (A) {$A$};
\node[above] at (B) {$B$};
\node[above left, xshift=-3pt] at (C) {$C$};
\node[below] at (D) {$D$};
\node[right] at (E) {$E$};
\pic[draw, "$93^{\circ}$", angle radius=0.4cm, angle eccentricity=2] {angle = E--C--D};
\pic[draw, "$x$", angle radius=0.45cm, angle eccentricity=2] {angle = B--A--D};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$ABCD$ is a cyclic quadrilateral.
$\angle DAB = 99^{\circ}$, $\angle ABC = 91^{\circ}$ and $\angle BCD = 81^{\circ}$.
Find $\angle CDA$.
[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{angles, quotes}
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (A) at (1.06,1.696);
\coordinate (B) at (-0.278,1.981);
\coordinate (C) at (-1.118,-1.658);
\coordinate (D) at (0.877,-1.798);
\draw (A) -- (B);
\draw (B) -- (C);
\draw (C) -- (D);
\draw (D) -- (A);
\draw (O) circle (2);
\node[above right, xshift=3pt] at (A) {$A$};
\node[above] at (B) {$B$};
\node[below left, xshift=-3pt] at (C) {$C$};
\node[below] at (D) {$D$};
\pic[draw, angle radius=0.45cm] {angle = B--A--D};
\node at (0.5,0.65) {$99^{\circ}$};
\pic[draw, angle radius=0.45cm] {angle = C--B--A};
\node[anchor=west] at (-0.35,1.35) {$91^{\circ}$};
\pic[draw, "$81^{\circ}$", angle radius=0.45cm, angle eccentricity=2] {angle = D--C--B};
\pic[draw, "$x$", angle radius=0.45cm, angle eccentricity=2] {angle = A--D--C};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

