$ABCD$ is a cyclic quadrilateral, and side $AB$ is extended to $E$.
$\angle DAB = 94^{\circ}$ and the exterior angle $\angle CBE = 79^{\circ}$.
Find $\angle BCD$ and $\angle CDA$.
[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{angles, quotes}
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (A) at (1.509,1.312);
\coordinate (B) at (0.651,1.891);
\coordinate (C) at (-1.891,-0.651);
\coordinate (D) at (-0.382,-1.963);
\draw (A) -- (B);
\draw (B) -- (C);
\draw (C) -- (D);
\draw (D) -- (A);
\draw (O) circle (2);
\coordinate (E) at (0.136,2.238);
\draw (B) -- (E);
\node[above right, xshift=3pt] at (A) {$A$};
\node[above] at (B) {$B$};
\node[left, xshift=-3pt] at (C) {$C$};
\node[below] at (D) {$D$};
\node[above right] at (E) {$E$};
\pic[draw, "$94^{\circ}$", angle radius=0.45cm, angle eccentricity=2] {angle = B--A--D};
\pic[draw, angle radius=0.4cm] {angle = E--B--C};
\node (label79) at (-1,2.8) {$79^{\circ}$};
\draw[->] (label79.south east) -- (0.253,1.856);
\pic[draw, "$x$", angle radius=0.45cm, angle eccentricity=2] {angle = D--C--B};
\pic[draw, "$y$", angle radius=0.45cm, angle eccentricity=2] {angle = A--D--C};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
